From a8dc58c25835d165ce7129c3877d35b707a8b28a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 19:33:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Table arm: prose cut into columns is not drafted as a table

pdfplumber's text strategy lays a column grid over running prose and
returns it as a table: 17 of 23 drafts on 9789240116191-eng and 23 of 45
on 9789240101197-eng were pages of prose with words cut at the cell
boundaries ('relat' | 'ionship'). A candidate whose boundaries cut a word
at a quarter or more of at least five side-by-side cell pairs is no
longer drafted, and the extraction note counts it apart from the other
dropped candidates.

Measured on the re-ingest pilot (2026-11-14, 109 candidates): every
grid a reader would call a table scored 0.12 or less, every page of
prose 0.42 or more. Kept on the two handbooks: 6 and 22 tables, the same
as a reading by hand.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VQDpPfb62Puokdy7SvkiNR
